WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.980
<b>Christmas Lottery</b>

00:09.730 --> 00:14.240
<b>Infinity Power</b>

00:10.060 --> 00:12.510
Please do these hair highlights.

00:13.110 --> 00:13.960
All right.

00:18.720 --> 00:21.480
When you're done with those, 
this needs finishing touches.

00:21.500 --> 00:24.000
Deadline!!

00:21.920 --> 00:22.920
Okay.

00:25.150 --> 00:27.500
A few more and all the 
backgrounds will be done.

00:28.620 --> 00:31.010
Stick with me through the homestretch!

00:31.260 --> 00:32.650
We can do it!

00:44.230 --> 00:51.530
Looks like it started before I knew it

00:52.280 --> 00:57.320
Thanks to you, I'm all smiles

00:59.240 --> 01:07.290
The usual townscape lends 
charm to the two of us

01:07.290 --> 01:12.800
Funny how it looks like a starry sky

01:16.550 --> 01:18.640
Suddenly buying flowers

01:18.640 --> 01:20.640
Standing around in the kitchen

01:20.640 --> 01:23.850
Sending a photo, because 
the setting sun is pretty

01:23.850 --> 01:28.400
Trying to spend as much 
time with you as I can

01:28.400 --> 01:31.400
This is all new for me

01:33.280 --> 01:38.950
I hope tomorrow is like today

01:39.280 --> 01:45.500
I've never felt this way before

01:45.500 --> 01:51.090
We'll go on a date this weekend if possible

01:51.750 --> 01:57.010
But it's fine if we stay home

01:58.260 --> 02:01.470
I can't wait to see you

02:03.970 --> 02:08.980
<b><b>Episode 8</b></b>

02:03.970 --> 02:08.980
<b><b>Christmas</b></b>

02:03.970 --> 02:08.980
<b><b>with the Princess</b></b>

02:12.410 --> 02:15.340
D-Done!

02:15.340 --> 02:17.490
We did it!

02:19.150 --> 02:22.120
Sorry things got so busy again.

02:22.420 --> 02:27.740
No, I'm glad to have experienced 
a "hellish year-end schedule."

02:27.750 --> 02:32.500
<b>Afternoon Sunny Wave</b>

02:28.690 --> 02:30.870
<i>It's </i>Afternoon Sunny Wave!

02:32.050 --> 02:34.520
<i>Christmas is almost here.</i>

02:34.520 --> 02:37.280
<i>We've been getting winter song requests.</i>

02:38.390 --> 02:41.500
<i>Oh right, Christmas!</i>

02:50.740 --> 02:52.520
<i>Lovely.</i>

02:54.170 --> 02:56.390
Um, are you...

02:57.120 --> 02:58.140
Yes?

02:58.140 --> 03:02.160
Do you have any Chr... N-New Year's plans?

03:02.160 --> 03:04.050
Like, going home to the island?

03:04.750 --> 03:07.530
I don't. I'm going to spend it here.

03:09.450 --> 03:12.050
Uh, is that a problem?

03:12.360 --> 03:15.540
Not at all. Let's greet 
the new year together.

03:15.970 --> 03:18.270
That's a lovely idea!

03:19.740 --> 03:21.340
Work's done.

03:21.340 --> 03:22.290
What's going on?

03:22.810 --> 03:25.120
Oh, we were talking about New Year's plans.

03:25.120 --> 03:27.820
I figured she could join us 
for the shrine visit, etc.

03:30.270 --> 03:32.390
We've got Christmas first!

03:32.390 --> 03:33.190
First.

03:33.540 --> 03:35.190
Christmas!

03:35.730 --> 03:38.540
Don't tell me you don't know about it?

03:38.540 --> 03:40.790
No, I do know.

03:40.790 --> 03:43.940
We don't really celebrate it back home.

03:44.590 --> 03:46.940
But I have Christmas knowledge!

03:47.340 --> 03:51.450
Okay, but be careful because 
Fumio still believes in Santa.

03:52.190 --> 03:54.270
When you say Santa...

03:55.000 --> 03:58.400
you mean the old man who 
sneaks in with presents.

03:58.700 --> 04:00.700
You don't believe anymore?

04:00.700 --> 04:03.980
Right, there's no Santa. Not in Japan.

04:04.360 --> 04:08.290
He's from overseas, so he can't 
make it here every time.

04:08.290 --> 04:13.550
Every kid can get a gift once from the 
real Santa-san by the time they're ten,

04:13.550 --> 04:16.110
but I already got mine.

04:17.700 --> 04:20.600
You don't say. What gift was that?

04:22.630 --> 04:23.610
Fumio!

04:23.920 --> 04:25.490
Oh, how lovely!

04:26.060 --> 04:29.660
Christmas is special for the Kuga family.

04:29.660 --> 04:32.220
Yeah! We also have a Christmas party.

04:32.220 --> 04:33.480
Let's have it together!

04:33.480 --> 04:35.510
I'd love to!

04:36.880 --> 04:40.250
<i>This could be for better or for worse.</i>

04:43.240 --> 04:45.210
<i>Oh, well.</i>

04:49.570 --> 04:52.260
Merry Christmas Eve!

04:52.760 --> 04:54.990
Moka-nee! Come on in!

04:54.990 --> 04:56.280
Come in.

04:56.280 --> 04:58.340
Thank you for inviting me.

04:58.850 --> 05:00.290
Here are some refreshments.

05:00.290 --> 05:01.270
Thank you!

05:08.330 --> 05:10.780
Beefcake-sensei! It's been a while!

05:10.780 --> 05:12.840
Yeah, it has.

05:13.800 --> 05:15.920
For us too, Sano-kun!

05:17.700 --> 05:19.960
Did you grow some?

05:20.750 --> 05:21.670
Thought so.

05:22.050 --> 05:24.000
Sano-sensei!

05:24.970 --> 05:26.810
I appreciate all the work.

05:26.810 --> 05:29.430
M-My thoughts exactly.

05:29.430 --> 05:31.800
You and Fumio-san get along well.

05:33.140 --> 05:35.580
W-Well, I was invited to the Christmas party

05:35.580 --> 05:38.560
the whole time I was an assistant, 
which ended last year.

05:38.560 --> 05:43.030
Don't you have a manga volume coming 
out soon? I'm looking forward to it.

05:43.030 --> 05:45.390
Oh, I'll give you a comp copy.

05:45.390 --> 05:46.830
I already bought one in advance.

05:48.430 --> 05:53.440
Sorry, sorry. I was just so happy that someone 
who'd helped me was going to debut.

05:53.840 --> 05:56.140
It's not such a huge deal.

06:00.350 --> 06:02.060
Cheers!

06:02.680 --> 06:04.320
Yummy!

06:04.320 --> 06:05.460
Yum!

06:05.740 --> 06:10.460
It's not the first time I've noticed, 
but Kuga-san is good at cooking.

06:10.720 --> 06:12.960
I can't do it without a recipe.

06:12.960 --> 06:14.850
Don't be modest.

06:14.850 --> 06:18.640
I just wanted you to know 
I think you're wonderful.

06:18.640 --> 06:20.220
I'm just embarrassed.

06:20.840 --> 06:22.230
Th-Thank you.

06:22.230 --> 06:24.740
Listen to the lovebirds.

06:28.430 --> 06:30.050
You're dating?!

06:30.870 --> 06:32.110
Yes.

06:34.370 --> 06:36.990
I was the one who confessed.

06:37.180 --> 06:39.080
Wow...

06:39.390 --> 06:41.720
To Ichiro-kun, huh?

06:42.150 --> 06:44.750
You said it. I was surprised, too.

06:45.150 --> 06:49.520
Well, Ichiro-kun's a good guy. I get it.

06:50.570 --> 06:52.520
Y-You think so?

06:53.130 --> 06:55.510
I'd like to hear stories about him.

06:55.510 --> 06:57.020
Stop it.

06:57.230 --> 07:02.510
Once, when I fell down and 
was bleeding all over...

07:03.630 --> 07:06.640
That really hurts! Let's take a picture!

07:06.640 --> 07:10.160
No! What if it gets infected?!

07:14.200 --> 07:19.100
Shy Ichiro-kun got seriously 
angry out of concern.

07:19.600 --> 07:21.050
I was impressed.

07:22.000 --> 07:24.540
It's because you were bleeding so much.

07:25.060 --> 07:28.290
<i>I didn't know she felt that way about it.</i>

07:28.290 --> 07:29.790
Lovely!

07:29.790 --> 07:32.410
More stories like that, please!

07:34.380 --> 07:37.550
I bet Chihiro-san must have 
some, being his cousin.

07:38.130 --> 07:40.070
I think we've heard enough.

07:40.070 --> 07:41.450
Let's see...

07:41.450 --> 07:43.070
D-Don't go out of your way!

07:43.070 --> 07:45.330
I had just gotten into the high school here.

07:45.330 --> 07:48.090
I was glad, since it was 
the one I hoped to attend,

07:48.090 --> 07:50.940
but I had to move away 
from my family to do it.

07:53.230 --> 07:54.930
But when my parents told me

07:54.930 --> 07:59.280
that Ichiro-kun would look after me here 
during my three years of high school...

07:59.720 --> 08:01.190
I was really happy.

08:02.080 --> 08:05.830
No, that was because you were studying so hard.

08:06.090 --> 08:09.330
So, that's how it happened. Lovely.

08:09.730 --> 08:11.340
I have one, too!

08:11.690 --> 08:14.350
Enough! This is too embarrassing!

08:14.750 --> 08:18.540
He always lets me and Fumio go first.

08:18.540 --> 08:20.090
Even with food and baths.

08:20.090 --> 08:22.340
Because he loves us!

08:22.340 --> 08:24.790
That's all ordinary stuff.

08:25.220 --> 08:26.850
What's with this party?

08:27.120 --> 08:31.250
Compliments make him self-conscious! 
That's irresistible!

08:31.650 --> 08:33.860
Christmas is such a good time.

08:33.860 --> 08:36.560
Maybe I sh-should say something, too.

08:36.560 --> 08:37.740
That's okay!

08:38.680 --> 08:41.660
Then let's talk about Goshiki-san next.

08:41.660 --> 08:43.250
Where are you from, again?

08:43.580 --> 08:45.550
A place called Yobijima.

08:45.550 --> 08:49.380
You're from an island! 
What kind of place is Yobijima?

08:49.380 --> 08:53.140
Let's see... The people are 
all very kind and friendly.

08:53.410 --> 08:56.070
The stars look beautiful from there.

08:56.070 --> 08:58.930
Stars, huh? Nice!

08:58.930 --> 09:01.540
Sounds a lot more amazing than Tokyo!

09:01.540 --> 09:03.410
It truly is beautiful.

09:04.440 --> 09:06.820
I'd like to hear more about it.

09:06.820 --> 09:08.890
Like about your memories from there.

09:08.890 --> 09:10.370
Memories...

09:11.590 --> 09:13.650
<i>Wh-What should I say?</i>

09:14.520 --> 09:17.350
<i>They're nearly all memories 
of being the princess.</i>

09:22.070 --> 09:26.580
<i>And should I have been misrepresenting 
myself in the first place?</i>

09:27.300 --> 09:29.570
Oh hey, sorry.

09:30.160 --> 09:32.330
Maybe it was awkward to ask.

09:32.330 --> 09:34.600
No, it's not like that.

09:34.600 --> 09:36.050
Oh, I know.

09:36.300 --> 09:37.110
Here.

09:38.970 --> 09:41.840
The tablet. Sorry it took so long.

09:41.840 --> 09:44.530
But now it's a Christmas present.

09:44.530 --> 09:46.380
This is the tablet?

09:47.520 --> 09:49.600
Thank you!

09:49.600 --> 09:50.820
No problem.

09:51.510 --> 09:53.610
These are for Machi and Fumio.

09:53.610 --> 09:55.080
Yay!

09:56.060 --> 09:56.870
Thanks!

09:56.870 --> 09:57.790
Thanks.

09:58.760 --> 10:02.070
I had a great time! And the food was delicious.

10:02.080 --> 10:07.830
<b>Hiiragi Apartments</b>

10:02.550 --> 10:04.040
Be safe going home.

10:04.040 --> 10:05.020
Sure thing.

10:05.020 --> 10:07.830
Oh, is it also Happy New Year time?

10:08.130 --> 10:11.330
Right, this'll be our last 
time together this year.

10:11.330 --> 10:13.840
Yeah. Happy New Year.

10:14.710 --> 10:16.510
See you next year!

10:19.170 --> 10:23.340
"See you next year." 
Words that warm the heart.

10:24.990 --> 10:27.580
Hey, can we stay up a little later?

10:28.570 --> 10:30.600
Fumio says he's sleepy.

10:32.780 --> 10:35.600
I'd like to talk a bit more.

10:35.600 --> 10:37.630
I'll stay up with you, if you like.

10:38.300 --> 10:39.480
Yes!

10:40.390 --> 10:43.740
Chibi-chan, come hang out with us!

10:43.970 --> 10:46.240
Okay, want to come to my room?

10:47.020 --> 10:49.740
Hooray! Can I wear pajamas?

10:50.120 --> 10:53.750
Pajamas?! Does that make this a sleepover?!

10:53.750 --> 10:55.260
Um...

10:55.760 --> 10:59.700
<i>This is my chance to find out what 
kind of person Goshiki-san is!</i>

11:00.240 --> 11:01.140
Sure!

11:01.510 --> 11:03.740
That's okay with you?

11:04.830 --> 11:06.030
Yay!

11:06.030 --> 11:09.600
<i>I was thinking about inviting her on a walk.</i>

11:10.690 --> 11:12.530
<i>But oh well.</i>

11:15.650 --> 11:17.690
Here we are!

11:20.040 --> 11:23.990
What a lovely room. You like books, I see.

11:24.940 --> 11:27.550
Let me know if you'd like
 to borrow any of them.

11:27.550 --> 11:29.280
Would that be okay?

11:29.290 --> 11:37.760
Stepping on Shadows

11:29.290 --> 11:37.760
Masami Ono

11:29.760 --> 11:33.630
This is a series, so start 
with volume one if possible!

11:33.630 --> 11:36.250
It's a mystery, but its portrayal 
of the working world is good,

11:36.250 --> 11:37.750
and the characters are adorable!

11:40.270 --> 11:41.530
Sorry.

11:41.530 --> 11:42.760
I got excited.

11:42.760 --> 11:45.770
Hey, is it okay to open these cases?

11:46.580 --> 11:48.000
No, not those.

11:48.710 --> 11:50.260
Oh, sorry.

11:50.260 --> 11:53.100
<i>Wh-What's inside there?</i>

11:53.770 --> 11:55.760
Stepping on Shadows

11:53.770 --> 11:55.760
Masami Ono

11:54.680 --> 11:58.030
It's nice to receive a book recommendation.

11:58.030 --> 12:00.140
It's like we're close friends.

12:00.410 --> 12:02.650
Oh yes, true.

12:02.940 --> 12:07.650
Goshiki-san! We're having a sleepover. 
We're totally friends!

12:09.910 --> 12:12.630
Hey, there's no need to rush things.

12:12.630 --> 12:14.260
Friends.

12:15.380 --> 12:17.060
You're right, we are.

12:17.940 --> 12:19.410
Goshiki-san?

12:19.710 --> 12:22.640
<i>I hope those two aren't being unreasonable.</i>

12:22.940 --> 12:24.350
There's something...

12:26.540 --> 12:29.290
I haven't told the two of you.

12:32.570 --> 12:34.200
On my island...

12:35.960 --> 12:38.830
I was a princess!

12:48.970 --> 12:51.960
I was a princess.

12:51.960 --> 12:53.110
Prin...

12:53.110 --> 12:53.970
...cess.

12:54.660 --> 12:56.460
Yes, a princess.

12:58.650 --> 13:01.220
Because of said obligations, and my...

13:02.230 --> 13:08.320
...personal issues, it's been a 
burden on my boyfriend, Kuga-san.

13:08.670 --> 13:13.210
Keeping quiet about it makes me feel like 
I'm deceiving everyone, and that stings.

13:14.130 --> 13:16.720
<i>Oh, great. Now I'm eavesdropping.</i>

13:21.410 --> 13:24.550
That sounds like it's pretty bad,

13:24.550 --> 13:27.490
but are you thinking we're not friends 
if you don't tell us everything?

13:29.600 --> 13:33.490
I'll listen if you want to talk, 
but it's okay to keep it secret.

13:33.490 --> 13:35.300
I have secrets, too.

13:35.300 --> 13:36.810
You do?

13:36.810 --> 13:40.490
I even have things I haven't told... Ichiro.

13:41.500 --> 13:43.000
<i>She does?</i>

13:43.900 --> 13:47.520
I guess I have things I still 
want to keep secret, too.

13:47.830 --> 13:49.500
I see.

13:50.010 --> 13:51.510
Does Ichiro know?

13:52.060 --> 13:53.000
Yes.

13:53.260 --> 13:55.090
Then it's fine.

13:55.090 --> 13:58.520
He'll be your ally, just not 
a super strong one.

14:00.680 --> 14:04.020
As your friend, you have my 
permission to have secrets.

14:04.310 --> 14:07.020
Okay. Thank you.

14:07.020 --> 14:11.030
<i>Maybe Goshiki-san is sweeter than I thought.</i>

14:11.030 --> 14:13.190
Uh, may I call you "Shiori-san"?

14:13.190 --> 14:15.310
Can I call you "Shio-chan"?

14:15.310 --> 14:17.040
Yes, certainly!

14:19.040 --> 14:20.130
Shio-chan!

14:20.710 --> 14:21.750
Machi-chan.

14:23.400 --> 14:24.800
Shio... chan!

14:25.150 --> 14:26.300
Chihiro-chan.

14:32.540 --> 14:36.550
It's been a burden on my boyfriend, Kuga-san.

14:37.570 --> 14:41.400
<i>It bothers her... that much, huh.</i>

14:41.400 --> 14:45.700
<i>To be honest, at first there were times 
when I considered it just her problem.</i>

14:46.400 --> 14:50.450
Now you and my stinger have been linked.

14:52.630 --> 14:57.660
That amounts to the two of us vowing 
to bind our destinies together!

14:59.190 --> 15:05.080
You want to know if it's 
possible to annul our pact.

15:05.810 --> 15:07.080
<i>Is</i> it possible?

15:07.340 --> 15:13.190
I don't know yet, but I arranged for my 
staff on the island to look into it.

15:13.820 --> 15:17.000
<i>I've been waiting patiently 
for it to be resolved.</i>

15:17.000 --> 15:17.840
<i>But...</i>

15:21.290 --> 15:23.130
Santa brought us presents!

15:23.130 --> 15:24.360
Santa-san!

15:24.700 --> 15:26.870
Good for you.

15:27.190 --> 15:30.860
Castles of Japan

15:28.630 --> 15:30.870
It's a castle book! Way to go!

15:31.620 --> 15:33.870
I got a sticker maker!

15:34.830 --> 15:36.620
Good morning.

15:37.920 --> 15:39.720
Good morning, Shio-chan!

15:39.720 --> 15:42.450
U-Um, Goshiki-san...

15:42.790 --> 15:43.730
Yes?

15:45.560 --> 15:47.880
Do you have some time tonight?!

15:48.250 --> 15:49.380
Tonight!

15:49.380 --> 15:51.780
Once dinner is over...

15:51.780 --> 15:55.270
Aw, you can at least eat dinner with her.

15:55.270 --> 15:58.510
No way! We all eat dinner together!

15:59.090 --> 16:01.760
It's just that it's Christmas and all.

16:01.760 --> 16:03.410
Is this a date?

16:03.690 --> 16:05.260
That's right!

16:05.260 --> 16:07.140
A Christmas date!

16:08.250 --> 16:09.350
I'd love to!

16:15.660 --> 16:18.850
Miyako, it's chilly out here.

16:18.850 --> 16:22.280
Why not bring a coat, if you think so?

16:23.430 --> 16:25.820
Isn't today that Christmas thing?

16:26.380 --> 16:28.620
Shall we go out somewhere, for a change?

16:28.620 --> 16:31.710
Huh? You're free to go on your own.

16:31.710 --> 16:32.950
Got it.

16:36.200 --> 16:38.920
I wonder if Shiori's doing well.

16:39.650 --> 16:43.810
It's nearly the New Year, and she 
has yet to contact us at all.

16:45.020 --> 16:46.470
Do you miss her?

16:46.470 --> 16:51.310
My feelings aren't so simple as that.

17:04.840 --> 17:08.580
Shining lights as far as the 
eye can see. Lovely!

17:16.790 --> 17:19.100
I saw this in <i>Choco Life</i> volume four!

17:19.100 --> 17:22.100
A Christmas lights date!

17:23.020 --> 17:25.480
<i>I'm glad she's enjoying this.</i>

17:26.100 --> 17:32.090
They say the lights were originally candles 
placed on trees to represent stars.

17:32.090 --> 17:35.750
I guess the stars look prettier 
from your island, though.

17:36.120 --> 17:42.300
But these lights are at eye level rather 
than overhead, so they're more fascinating.

17:42.300 --> 17:44.250
It's like they're drawing me in.

17:45.530 --> 17:48.470
I haven't paid much attention 
to these things lately.

17:49.220 --> 17:52.740
But today, they seem 
prettier than usual.

17:53.550 --> 17:59.010
Does that mean it seems pretty because 
you're looking at it with me?

17:59.710 --> 18:01.500
Y-Yes...

18:03.590 --> 18:07.880
When we're like this, it's like 
there was never any problem.

18:07.880 --> 18:10.900
But every time I grow closer to you,

18:10.900 --> 18:16.950
the fact that the pact causes you pain
 jabs at me like a stinger.

18:17.360 --> 18:19.300
It makes me wonder if it should be this way.

18:21.580 --> 18:23.410
I mean, I'm...

18:23.410 --> 18:27.680
We've been careful to avoid any 
retribution from the pact lately.

18:27.680 --> 18:30.050
I thought we'd been doing well.

18:31.060 --> 18:33.530
But that doesn't mean it's gone.

18:33.820 --> 18:38.030
It's a problem that I must resolve.

18:38.030 --> 18:42.560
That makes it sound like it's your 
fault, and I don't like that.

18:44.560 --> 18:50.550
Let's think it over together, taking your 
family and physiology into consideration.

18:55.710 --> 18:57.700
Because I love you.

18:58.170 --> 19:03.210
I-I'm surprised you've 
given it that much thought.

19:03.500 --> 19:08.710
Yeah, that's why I want us to stop 
dating like we're trying it out.

19:11.500 --> 19:12.710
Would you...

19:14.710 --> 19:18.010
go out with me with the intent 
to someday get married?!

19:19.040 --> 19:23.890
And I also mean let's do away with 
the ancestral Engagement Pact thing.

19:23.890 --> 19:25.840
Of course, if you don't want to, it's fine!

19:28.500 --> 19:30.720
G-Goshiki-san?

19:30.980 --> 19:36.780
Um, is it all right if I kiss you?

19:41.260 --> 19:42.260
Now?!

19:42.260 --> 19:43.420
Wh-Where?!

19:43.420 --> 19:44.580
On the face.

19:44.580 --> 19:46.800
Face! F-Face, right.

19:49.510 --> 19:51.430
Y-Yes.

20:10.650 --> 20:12.180
Of course I want to.

20:12.770 --> 20:15.370
I love you.

20:21.740 --> 20:23.170
We're home.

20:24.040 --> 20:25.470
Welcome back.

20:25.840 --> 20:28.610
What, you came home this early?

20:28.610 --> 20:31.310
Yep, and we brought home a cake.

20:31.710 --> 20:33.070
Thanks!

20:33.430 --> 20:36.790
You two must have been cold. 
Your faces are beet red!

20:37.100 --> 20:39.440
No, we're warm.

20:41.180 --> 20:42.600
Let's have some cake.

20:42.600 --> 20:45.300
I-I'm going to go wash my hands and gargle.

20:54.030 --> 20:55.820
<i>I did it!</i>

20:58.580 --> 21:02.280
<i>Kuga-san's lips. That softness.</i>

21:04.050 --> 21:07.980
<i>Wait, </i>were<i> they soft? 
What were they like again?</i>

21:10.010 --> 21:14.140
<i>My eyes were closed, 
so was my aim a little off?</i>

21:14.140 --> 21:15.220
<i>Was it here?</i>

21:15.220 --> 21:16.380
<i>Or here?</i>

21:16.380 --> 21:17.850
<i>Or around here?</i>

21:18.100 --> 21:21.350
<i>How could this be?! I even 
had my hands on his face...</i>

21:21.940 --> 21:29.680
<i>But... but that time you might call an eternity,
 within me it was the longest moment.</i>

21:29.680 --> 21:30.470
<i>"Moment"?</i>

21:30.470 --> 21:31.970
Start

21:30.470 --> 21:31.970
Reset

21:36.780 --> 21:38.470
0.2 seconds?!

21:42.390 --> 21:45.380
But it felt as good as a 
two-page color spread!

21:45.380 --> 21:48.490
Next time it'll be longer. 
At least a second!

21:52.210 --> 21:53.990
<i>I can't sleep.</i>

21:58.250 --> 22:01.440
A second is so long!

22:04.890 --> 22:06.270
A message?

22:10.010 --> 22:12.510
<b>This is your mother.</b>

22:10.010 --> 22:12.510
<b>Inbox</b>

22:10.010 --> 22:12.510
<b>Mom</b>

22:16.060 --> 22:27.650
A long red thread stretching 
into the distance

22:27.650 --> 22:38.800
Meeting you, even if it meant having 
to cross hundreds of light-years

22:38.800 --> 22:45.480
Maybe I'll slowly get used to

22:45.480 --> 22:52.390
The two of us going out to have fun

22:52.390 --> 23:02.230
A tug on my arm, by the bond 
that was formed that day

23:02.230 --> 23:08.090
A little at a time, we've 
come closer together

23:08.090 --> 23:12.880
More smiles for us

23:12.880 --> 23:25.690
That place I first learned of, and 
the shops we'll visit again tomorrow

23:25.690 --> 23:31.650
They'll all be part of these lovely days

23:31.650 --> 23:38.490
Looking forward to it, good night

23:46.080 --> 23:48.410
I'd like to go to a hot spring for a change.

23:48.430 --> 23:49.580
For a change.

23:49.580 --> 23:51.950
But if wishes were fishes...

23:52.210 --> 23:52.890
Huh?

23:52.890 --> 23:53.610
Huh-huh?

23:53.610 --> 23:54.380
Huh-huh?

23:54.380 --> 23:55.700
Huh-huh-huh?

23:55.700 --> 23:57.110
Is it a you-know-what?

23:55.950 --> 23:59.950
<b><b>Episode 9</b></b>

23:55.950 --> 23:59.950
<b><b>A Hot Spring with the Princess</b></b>

23:57.110 --> 23:58.960
A hot spring trip!
